*Drawing to be made by the candidate: a large **longitudinal (sagittal) section of the human brain**, with a title ("L.S. of the mammalian brain"), sharp lines and label lines.*

**Parts to draw and label:**
- **Cerebrum** (cerebral hemispheres: the large, folded (convoluted) upper part, with the **corpus callosum** joining the two hemispheres);
- **Thalamus** and **hypothalamus** (centre of the brain, below the cerebrum);
- **Pituitary gland** (hangs below the hypothalamus);
- **Cerebellum** (at the back, below the cerebrum, finely folded; balance and coordination);
- **Pons** and **medulla oblongata** (brain stem, joined to the **spinal cord**; control breathing and heart rate);
- **Olfactory lobe** (front; smell);
- **Meninges** (protective membranes around the brain) and the **skull** (outer).
